# Adding per-chapter editors later
# --------------------------------
# When someone takes lasting responsibility for a run of sections, give them
# those paths. Later rules win, so put the specific ones below the catch-all:
#
#   /fa/24.md  @Kaaveh @some-editor
#   /fa/25.md  @Kaaveh @some-editor
#
# GitHub's CODEOWNERS has no range syntax, so a run of sections means one line
# each. That is tedious but explicit, which is the right trade for something
# that governs who can approve a change to the text.
#
# Keep @Kaaveh on text paths even when delegating: consistency of voice across
# the whole book is a maintainer responsibility and cannot be reviewed one
# chapter at a time.
#
# Tooling is different — it can be owned outright by whoever maintains it:
#
#   /tools/     @some-tooling-person
#   /.github/   @some-tooling-person
